                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "One of the best games ever made. 20 years ahead of its time. I still fondly reminisce the years of '06 to '14 when I was playing it with some mates. The Ship, TeamSpeak, pizza, and Coca-Cola from those old hard plastic 1.5 L bottles before they got force-softified by EU regulations. Going to lock 15 friends into a basement and force them to play it in 202X.\n\nGame has aged slightly poorly and is prone to crash (on my machine at least):\n- Some of the bigger maps crash on loading screen, unless you increase the allocated memory via launch parameters*:\n[b]-heapsize 1048576[/b] should do the trick.\n- Alt-tabbing crashes the game occasionally.\n- Other random crashes may still occur.\nBarely any servers. Absolutely no players. [b]Bots aka [i]Shipmates[/i] are available though.[/b]\nThere are some gameplay quirks that are lowkey exploits. [spoiler]Don't use +zoom or you're lame.[/spoiler]",
